# Generated from the OSRS Wiki page "Transcript:Haunted Mine" by tools/quests/transcript_to_dialogue.py
0	section	Starting out
1	line	Player	Hello there. What are you doing here?
1	line	Player	Hello there.
1	line	Zealot	State thy allegiance stranger.
1	select	Select an option
1	option	I follow the path of Saradomin.
2	line	Player	I follow the path of Saradomin. Strength through wisdom.
2	line	Zealot	Ah, a wise choice my friend. But if you truly follow Saradomin, what brings you to these evil lands?
2	select	Select an option
2	option	I come seeking challenges and quests.
3	line	Player	I come seeking challenges and quests.
3	line	Zealot	A noble cause indeed. One that I can sympathise with, for I myself am upon a quest. One that will allow Saradomin to be glorified even in these dark lands.
3	select	Start the Haunted Mine quest?
3	option	Yes.
4	line	Player	What quest is that then?
4	line	Zealot	Well, below the very ground you stand upon lies an intricate network of tunnels that make up the abandoned Mort Ridge mines. These mines used to be a valuable resource to the inhabitants of Morytania.
4	line	Zealot	As with many things, this changed when Misthalin was finally able to push the minions of Morytania back, and Saradomin himself blessed the river Salve.
4	line	Zealot	The mines are also the site where the legendary artefact, the salve amulet, was thought to have been carved from the crystals that grow in the lower levels of the mine.
4	line	Zealot	These crystals are thought to be formed by the blessed water of the river Salve as it percolates through the rocks to the lower levels of the mine.
4	line	Zealot	It is not known what happened to the salve amulet, but it is generally believed that by encapsulating within it some of the goodness of Saradomin himself, it afforded the bearer power over evil.
4	line	Zealot	Saradomin has entrusted me alone with the task of regaining access to the mines, whatever the dangers.
4	line	Player	How can an abandoned mine be dangerous?
4	line	Zealot	Because the mines are said to be haunted. The crystals and the ridge used to be protected by Zamorak's mage, Treus Dayth.
4	line	Zealot	Dayth failed and fell during an incursion by Saradominists, who then made it into the mines and were able to remove a shard of crystal.
4	line	Zealot	Zamorak, furious at his mage, condemned Dayth's soul indefinitely to an existence of turmoil in the mines. Dayth's soul is bound to prevent the crystals from ever being reached again.
4	line	Zealot	Further, Zamorak's then ruler upon the land ordered the slaughter of anyone within the mines and that the mines be sealed.
4	select	Select an option
4	option	Is there any other way into the mines?
5	action	below
4	option	How does a lost artefact that was only legendary help?
5	action	below
4	option	Why was everyone in the mines slaughtered?
5	action	below
4	option	I must be going now.
5	line	Player	I must be going now, good luck on your quest.
5	line	Zealot	You should believe not in luck, but in the protection of Saradomin. Farewell.
5	action	end
3	option	No.
4	line	Player	I hope it goes well. Goodbye.
4	line	Zealot	Goodbye, and may Saradomin give you strength through wisdom.
4	action	end
2	option	Ok I lied.
3	line	Player	Ok I lied, I don't support Saradomin. I'm only here for dastardly evil purposes.
3	line	Zealot	Then leave me, I have no time to listen to your poisonous tongue.
3	action	end
2	option	I could ask the same of you.
3	line	Player	I could ask the same of you.
3	line	Zealot	Saradomin has granted you wisdom. The evil creatures of this land are cunning and you are right to question anyone's purpose here.
3	line	Zealot	I am upon a quest. One that will allow Saradomin to be glorified even in these dark lands.
3	action	above
1	option	I serve only Zamorak.
2	line	Player	I serve only Zamorak. Strength through chaos.
2	line	Zealot	Then begone. Normally I would strike you down in an instant, but for now I have no time. I am on a quest of the utmost importance.
2	select	Select an option
2	option	What is this quest of which you speak?
3	line	Player	What is this quest of which you speak?
3	line	Zealot	It is no concern of yours, but rest assured it will help in crushing you and those others who serve your vile master.
3	line	Player	I doubt that.
3	line	Zealot	I would expect nothing less of you, misguided as you already are.
3	action	end
2	option	Fine, I didn't want to talk to you either.
3	line	Player	Fine, I didn't want to talk to you either.
3	line	Zealot	Fear not fiend, even though I may leave you be, you shall not escape justice at the hands of the righteous.
3	action	end
1	option	My beliefs are in accord with the teachings of Guthix.
2	line	Player	My beliefs are in accord with the teachings of Guthix. Balance is power.
2	line	Zealot	A wishy washy set of beliefs. You should follow Saradomin and find a real purpose in your life.
2	select	Select an option
2	option	And what sort of purpose would that be?
3	line	Player	And what sort of purpose would that be?
3	line	Zealot	To further the glory of Saradomin of course.
3	line	Zealot	Take myself, I am upon a quest that will allow Saradomin to be glorified even in these dark lands.
3	action	above
2	option	I can make my own choices.
3	line	Player	I can make my own choices, who are you to dispute them?
3	line	Zealot	I look only to help those who are misguided.
3	action	end
1	option	I have no particular allegiance.
2	line	Player	I have no particular allegiance.
2	line	Zealot	Then your life is without reason or direction. I would talk to you further on the matter, but for now my attentions must be elsewhere.
2	select	Select an option
2	option	Then I shall leave you to your business.
3	line	Player	Then I shall leave you to your business.
3	line	Zealot	I shall pray that Saradomin grants you the wisdom to see through your folly.
3	action	end
