0	section	Talking to the zealot again
1	line	Player	Hello there.
1	line	Zealot	Hello again. I'm afraid I'm rather preoccupied. What was it you wanted?
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Can you explain the history of these mines again?
2	line	Player	Can you explain the history of these mines again?
2	action	above
1	option	Is there any other way into the mines?
2	line	Player	Is there any other way into the mines?
2	line	Zealot	Indeed I have found hope that this may be so. By making discreet inquiries I have been led to believe that a second entrance may exist into the mines.
2	line	Zealot	Further, I have come into possession of a key that will apparently afford entrance to the lower levels of the mines once inside.
2	select	Select an option
2	option	Where is the second entrance to the mines?
3	line	Player	Where is the second entrance to the mines?
3	line	Zealot	Of this I am not yet sure. From what I have been able to gather, it was not originally built for humans to enter by. Where it may be, I am still endeavoring to find out.
3	action	initial
2	option	How can you be discreet with THAT star emblazoned on your robes?
3	line	Player	How can you be discreet with THAT star emblazoned on your robes?
3	line	Zealot	Saradomin watches over me, I am not troubled by those who are not meant to notice.
3	line	Player	Even so, you're not exactly keeping quiet about your allegiance are you?
3	line	Zealot	Saradomin will protect me. Even if I should fall there are many behind me who would stand in my place.
3	select	Select an option
3	option	Is that much consolation?
4	line	Player	Is that much consolation when you get chopped up into little pieces?
4	line	Zealot	I would rather be cut into little pieces whilst proclaiming the goodness of Saradomin than hiding my faith.
4	action	end
3	option	I can't see anyone behind you.
4	line	Player	I can't see anyone behind you.
4	line	Zealot	Although you may not realise it, Saradomin works quietly in many people, such is the folly of looking with your eyes and not with your heart.
4	action	end
3	option	And I would be one of them. So, can I borrow that key?
4	line	Player	And I would be one of them. So, can I borrow that key?
4	line	Zealot	I am afraid my task can be entrusted to nobody else. Saradomin has asked me alone to do this. I cannot take the slightest risk of losing this key. The stakes are too high.
4	select	Select an option
4	option	Please? I'll be very careful with it.
5	action	below
4	option	I didn't want that key anyway.
5	action	below
3	option	You're right, I was wrong to doubt Saradomin.
4	line	Player	You're right, I was wrong to doubt Saradomin.
4	line	Zealot	Let not your faith in Saradomin falter, for all else is insignificant.
4	action	end
3	option	You're nuts, goodbye.
4	line	Player	You're nuts, goodbye.
4	action	end
2	option	Can I borrow your key?
3	line	Player	Can I borrow your key?
3	line	Zealot	I am afraid my task can be entrusted to nobody else. Saradomin has asked me alone to do this. I cannot take the slightest risk of losing this key. The stakes are too high.
3	select	Select an option
3	option	Please? I'll be very careful with it.
4	line	Player	Please? I'll be very careful with it.
4	line	Zealot	You know not what you deal with. There is evil in that mine and, whatever your assurances, I cannot risk you falling to the creatures within.
4	select	Select an option
4	option	And you think you'll be safer in the mine than me?
5	line	Player	And you think you'll be safer in the mine than me?
5	line	Zealot	Of course I'll be safe, my faith in Saradomin protects me.
5	action	end
4	option	I'll trade for it.
5	line	Player	I'll trade for it.
5	line	Zealot	Saradomin provides for my every need. There is nothing you could offer me.
5	action	end
4	option	Pretty pretty please?
5	line	Player	Pretty pretty please?
5	line	Zealot	Saradomin grant me patience. The answer is no.
5	action	end
4	option	I didn't want that key anyway.
5	action	below
3	option	I didn't want that key anyway.
4	line	Player	I didn't want that key anyway.
4	line	Zealot	Witness the goodness of Saradomin, that he has granted you the wisdom to see our positions in perspective.
4	action	end
