0	section	Talking to the zealot after encountering Treus Dayth
1	line	Player	G... g... g... ghost! Scary ghost! Machinery flying everywhere.
1	line	Zealot	I warned you not to enter those mines. It sounds like you've met Dayth. You must not go back down there.
1	select	Select an option
1	option	Who did you say Dayth was again?
2	line	Player	Who did you say Dayth was again?
2	line	Zealot	Treus Dayth was Zamorak's mage in charge of defending the ridge during the time of the orginal amulet.
2	line	Zealot	Dayth failed and fell during an incursion by Saradominists, who then made it into the mines and were able to remove a shard of crystal.
2	line	Zealot	Zamorak, furious at his mage, condemned Dayth's soul indefinitely to an existence of turmoil in the mines. Dayth's soul is bound to prevent the crystals from ever being reached again.
2	action	end
1	option	Nonsense, he'll be no match for me.
2	line	Player	Nonsense, he'll be no match for me.
2	line	Zealot	I don't know if you think your persistance makes you heroic, but you must realise it's just going to get you killed.
2	action	end
0	section	Talking to the zealot after killing Treus Dayth
1	line	Player	I met that Dayth character you talked about. He wasn't as tough as all that.
1	line	Zealot	I was afraid this would happen. The fear you must have experienced within those mines has left you delusional. There's no way you could have survived had you actually fought Dayth.
1	action	end
